  // If n is odd, x is determined. we can expand a and try to match a'.
  // The hard part is when n is even.
  // Note that we can consider each bit independently.
  // Then the problem becomes: given a 01 sequence A of length 2*n-1, try to
  // match another 01 sequnce B of length N in A. Then flip all bits of A and do
  // the match again. Note that if K is a shift for the first search, it must
  // not be a shift for the second search where the text string is flipped, and
  // vice versa.
  int n;
  scan(n);
